sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Commensurable magnitudes have to one another the ratio which a number has to a number.
----
proof:

Let {A} and {B} be commensurable magnitudes.

I say that {A} has to {B} the ratio which a number has to a number.

Since {A} and {B} are commensurable, some magnitude {C} measures them.

As many times as {C} measures {A}, let so many units be in {D}, and, as many times as {C} measures {B}, let so many units be in {E}.

